  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine Response in Romania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To respond to the humanitarian crisis generated by conflict in Ukraine, Romanian Federation of Community Foundations (RFCF) and Community Foundations (CFs) worked towards urgently identified needs. On short and medium term, the CFs network plans to address integration issues in the following areas: Area 1. Communication Campaigns: promoting cohesion, participation in the community (education, job market) and peaceful communication messages by working with media outlets and journalists for building awareness. Area 2. Education: integrating children in educational activities and programs. Area 3. Social Cohesion: mixing and bringing together hosting communities and refugees within programs and activities initiated by local organisations.  Within this vast range of needs, Oxfam together with its partners prioritises:  Access to accurate, safe and up -to -date information.  Access to safe, secure and dignified housing,  Access to basic and specialized services (incl. healthcare, mental health and psychosocial support, legal aid)  Access to cash assistance  Access to sexual and reproductive health and rights (incl. gender Based Violence (GBV) services)  Access to child -friendly spaces (incl. non -formal education and recreational activities)  Access to livelihoods</narrative>
  </description>
